          "text": "Clinical Indication  \nGeneralized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 8 years, currently occurring approximately 6 times per week. Etiology is unknown. Seizures are drug-resistant. Current antiseizure medications are zonisamide and carbamazepine.\n\nTechnique  \nRoutine digital scalp EEG performed using the international 10–20 electrode placement system.\n\nFindings  \nNo authorized EEG waveform findings were provided; therefore, the background, interictal activity, and ictal activity cannot be characterized.\n\nImpression  \nEEG interpretation is indeterminate because no waveform findings are available. The generalized epilepsy and generalized tonic-clonic seizure classification above reflects the clinical history and is not inferred from this EEG.",
